Q1. JPA, ORM and Hibernate basics
Ans: 
1. ORM
- ORM is general programming concept
- It maps java object to database tables and vice versa.
- It allows you to work with objects instead of writing raw SQL
- Exists in many languages and framework
Example:
A User class in java <---> user table in database

ORM handles:
- Converting objects to rows (INSERT)
- Fetching rows into object (SELECT)
- Updating/deleting records

ORM is just the approach, not a specific library.


2. JPA
JPA is a Java Specification for ORM.
 - Defined by Java
 - Provides standard interfaces and annotations
 - Does not do the actual work itself

Popular implementations of JPA:
Hibernate ORM, EclipseLink

Example:
@Entity
public class User {
	@Id
	private Long id;
	Private String name;	
	}

Here,
- @Entity @Id come from JPA
- Actual DB interaction is done by Hibernate.

ORM vs JPA

ORM is concept/Technic while JPA is Specification(Java Standard)
ORM is language-independent while JPA is Java-Specific
ORM role is to Map object to tables while JPA defines how ORM should work.

